session:pr505Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #42 asked for CodeMirror 6 syntax highlighting on the plain <textarea id=\"query\"> in sparql_endpoint/src/frontend.html, which is a single static HTML file with no build step (npm/webpack/vite) anywhere in the repo. A prior attempt on this branch stalled mid-task waiting on a background build/monitor rather than working synchronously; this session picked the branch back up, found the CodeMirror integration already committed and pushed (dbb3914) and PR #505 already open with all CI checks green, so the remaining work was verification rather than implementation. Key design choice, made by the earlier work and confirmed sound here: load CodeMirror 6 as ES modules directly from esm.sh (no bundler), keep the original textarea in the DOM as a hidden fallback wired through new getQueryValue()/setQueryValue() helpers so every existing call site (templates, query history, query builder, ?query= URL param, sample data) keeps working whether or not the CDN module loads. This session verified the concrete risk areas a text-only review can't skip: (1) all four esm.sh import URLs return HTTP 200; (2) both inline <script> blocks parse cleanly under `node --check`; (3) crucially, the include_str!-embedded frontend.html only picks up source changes on a *touch+rebuild* of sparql_endpoint (a first `cargo build -p dagalog` silently served a stale cached page missing every CodeMirror marker) — after touching frontend.rs/frontend.html and rebuilding, curling the running `dagalog --serve` binary confirmed the served page is byte-identical to the working tree and contains the CodeMirror mount div, imports, and dagalogQueryEditor wiring verbatim. Full quality gate (fmt/clippy/test --workspace) passed with zero Rust source changes, since this is an HTML/JS-only PR. What remains unverifiable in this headless environment, called out explicitly in the PR body, is actual browser rendering/highlighting/interaction — the graceful-degradation design (persistent fallback textarea, single read/write choke point) is the mitigation for that gap rather than a substitute for it." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:505 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr505 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
